            "Type": "TimerRestart",
            "Name": "AT_Ice_King_ManyPlayers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "$Comment": "AT_CIRCLE 1/2: move the leash point onto the target every tick (target within 60 blocks; 40 until 2026-10-21, past it the leash point stayed behind and the soft leash pulled him away) (SetLeashPosition ToTarget), so WanderInCircle below circles around the player, not around where the king spawned (BodyMotionWanderInCircle.getReferencePoint = NPCEntity.getLeashPoint).",
        "Continue": true,
        "Sensor": {
          "Type": "Target",
          "Range": 60
        },
        "Actions": [
          {
            "Type": "SetLeashPosition",
            "ToTarget": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "$Comment": "2026-10-21 (playtest: the ray still went where he was not): while he casts, turn the body toward the target. The circle already stops during a cast, but the template Seek that took over does nothing inside CombatSeekStopDistance, and a flier then keeps flying straight (MotionControllerFly, MinAirSpeed), so the head (Camera yaw +-60 from the body) still could not reach the player. MatchLook sets the body yaw to the head yaw every tick (BodyMotionMatchLook), so the body chases the aiming head until it faces the player; the first body motion of the tick wins, so it beats the Seek. Flight turn 180 deg/s, the ray leaves 0.8 s into the cast.",
        "Continue": true,
        "Sensor": {
          "Type": "And",
          "Sensors": [
            {
              "Type": "Target",
              "Range": 60
            },
            {
              "Type": "Self",
              "Filters": [
                {
                  "Type": "IsExecutingInteraction"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "BodyMotion": {
          "Type": "MatchLook"
        },
        "HeadMotion": {
          "Type": "Aim",
          "HitProbability": 1,
          "Spread": 0,
          "Deflection": false
        }
      },
      {
        "$Comment": "AT_ORBIT (2026-10-22: he hovered right over his head, he had to aim almost straight up; 40-50 degrees wanted). Replaces the WanderInCircle (radius 24), which picks random points INSIDE the circle and so crossed over the player; an AT_RING Flee tried the same day made him fly at ground level and was removed. Now 8 waypoints on a ring of radius 19 around the player, 19 blocks above him, so about 45 degrees up (horizontal distance = height). Each is the target's position plus an offset (AdjustPosition wrapping the Target sensor, as vanilla Template_Goblin_Scrapper wraps ReadPosition; the And sensor takes the first position, SensorAnd), flown to with the same Seek as the template's combat Seek (DesiredAltitudeWeight 1). The repeating timer AT_Ice_King_Air_Orbit (24 s) picks one waypoint per 3 s in order, so he goes round the player. Not while he casts (MatchLook turns him toward the player then). The template's OverrideAltitude (16-22 over the ground) still runs. Continue, so the timers below still run. Tune: radius and height in each Offset, seconds per waypoint in the TimeRemainingRange slices. 2026-10-22 (log: the waypoint rules were active the whole time but he did not move toward them): Seek UsePathfinder false and SkipSteering false. BodyMotionFind skips steering when its probe says the goal is not reached in a straight line (shouldSkipSteering), then falls back to the pathfinder, which waits 3-5 s after a failed search (ThrottleDelayRange); the waypoint changes every 2-3 s, so he never got going. In open air pure steering is enough. 2026-10-22, later (playtest: now he gets stuck in trees): pure steering flies straight into canopies, so the pathfinder is back as a fallback (UsePathfinder true) while steering is still tried first (SkipSteering false), and a failed path search waits 0.5-1 s instead of 3-5 (ThrottleDelayRange).",
        "Continue": true,
